 "answer": "Singapore’s latest official readings I found—**6 p.m. on October 15**—showed **unhealthy air**: the 24-hour PSI was **121–186**, and 1-hour PM2.5 ranged from **95 to 208 µg/m³** across locations. The readings vary by area and may have changed since then. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-15-october-2026))\n\nAt locations where 1-hour PM2.5 is in the **High** band, NEA advises avoiding strenuous outdoor activity; people with chronic heart or lung conditions, older adults, pregnant people, and children should avoid outdoor activity for the next hour. Check NEA’s live haze readings for your area before heading out. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-15-october-2026))",
